Update an MLH project the connected user is a member of. Only the fields passed are changed; `built_with`, `ai_tools` and `extra_links` replace the stored list whole, so send the complete list, in the formats create_project describes. `screenshot_paths` adds up to 5 local PNG or JPEG files per call (2 MB each) and `removed_screenshot_ids` removes screenshots by the ids list_my_projects shows. MLH refuses the edit once an entry at the project's event is approved or wins, once that event's submission window closes, or while the user is not checked in where that event requires it. A 422 names the program requirements the project fails, joined with ". " (for example "Select at least one technology" when `built_with` is empty, or "One-line pitch is required" when the event requires a `short_description`). Requires a connected MLH account (connect_mlh_account).

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__devrelay_gateway__update_project(args: {
  // Replacement list of AI tool ids, in the format create_project describes
  ai_tools?: Array<string>;
  // Replacement list of technologies used; keep at least one, since many events reject a submitted project without it
  built_with?: Array<string>;
  // New live demo URL
  demo_live_url?: string;
  // New demo video URL on YouTube, Vimeo or Loom
  demo_video_url?: string;
  // New description
  description?: string;
  // Replacement list of up to 5 other links, each {label (optional), url}
  extra_links?: Array<{ label?: string; url: string; }>;
  // New project name
  name?: string;
  // MLH project id (UUID) from list_my_projects or create_project
  project_id: string;
  // Ids of screenshots to remove, from the project's screenshots in list_my_projects
  removed_screenshot_ids?: Array<string>;
  // Up to 5 local paths of PNG or JPEG screenshots to add, each at most 2 MB
  screenshot_paths?: Array<string>;
  // New one-line pitch, at most 140 characters
  short_description?: string;
  // New repository URL
  source_url?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"view_image","description":"View a local image file from the filesystem when visual inspection is needed. Use this for images already available on disk.

